{"run":"7b4c0d8b-b08d-4368-9f45-9f9e5fa4ecf1","note":"2026-11-05 real run (The Quiet Kid and the Turtle's Drums): script, the take's word timings (timeline captions) and the stored director list (the mock fallback the old worker made)","topic":"we live inside a giant turtle and a big bad wolf with an army of soldiers is hunting it","lengthSec":90,"title":"The Quiet Kid and the Turtle's Drums","lines":[{"part":"rule","text":"In this world, everyone inside the giant turtle has a drumbeat ticking in their wrist, except me."},{"part":"tour","text":"You see, a wolf and his army hunt our turtle."},{"part":"tour","text":"They can't see us in the shell."},{"part":"tour","text":"They only listen for ticking wrists."},{"part":"tour","text":"Get caught ticking, and they march you off before dawn."},{"part":"tour","text":"Mrs. Oddy got carried off mid-yawn last Tuesday."},{"part":"tour","text":"Her chair still sits there, waiting."},{"part":"tour","text":"Baker Bell wraps his tick in a sock now."},{"part":"tour","text":"Just in case."},{"part":"tour","text":"The mail carrier tiptoes with a pillow strapped to his wrist."},{"part":"me","text":"I'm Nell, the quiet kid with no tick."},{"part":"me","text":"My wrist is silent. Totally bare."},{"part":"me","text":"Everyone says I'm lucky."},{"part":"me","text":"I just feel left out."},{"part":"me","text":"But I hear the boots before anyone else."},{"part":"me","text":"I live in a tiny bunk with Grandpa."},{"part":"me","text":"His wrist ticks like a nervous clock."},{"part":"me","text":"He gave me his wind-up pocket watch once."},{"part":"me","text":"Brass. Heavy. Stopped for years."},{"part":"me","text":"I keep it in a drawer."},{"part":"until","text":"Until one night, my water cup shivered."},{"part":"until","text":"Thud. Thud. Thud."},{"part":"until","text":"Far-off boots, marching in the dark."},{"part":"until","text":"Torch beams swept down our street."},{"part":"until","text":"Long shadows slid across the shutters."},{"part":"until","text":"Wolf ears on every helmet."},{"part":"until","text":"Then the boots stopped outside our door."},{"part":"until","text":"Grandpa's wrist glowed. Tick. Tick. Tick."},{"part":"until","text":"A fist pounded the wood. Boom."},{"part":"discovery","text":"I squeezed one eye to a crack in the shutter."},{"part":"discovery","text":"The soldiers had passed Baker Bell's house."},{"part":"discovery","text":"His sock-wrapped wrist didn't turn a single head."},{"part":"discovery","text":"Then a drumbeat boomed from the next street."},{"part":"discovery","text":"Every helmet swiveled at once."},{"part":"discovery","text":"They didn't want ticking wrists."},{"part":"discovery","text":"They wanted the loudest tick."},{"part":"climax","text":"I yanked open the drawer and grabbed the watch."},{"part":"climax","text":"I ran to the tail-gate ledge."},{"part":"climax","text":"I cranked Grandpa's watch. Click. Click. Click."},{"part":"climax","text":"The tick roared like a thunderstorm."},{"part":"climax","text":"Every drum in town answered."},{"part":"climax","text":"Torches swung toward me."},{"part":"climax","text":"The soldiers marched for the noise."},{"part":"climax","text":"Row after row marched off the back door."},{"part":"climax","text":"Splash. Splash. Splash."},{"part":"closer","text":"At dawn, the street was quiet and empty."},{"part":"closer","text":"Baker Bell pulled the sock off his wrist."},{"part":"closer","text":"Grandpa's watch ticked softly on mine."},{"part":"closer","text":"Everyone here has a tick in their wrist."},{"part":"closer","text":"Mine just needed a better watch."}],"words":[["In",0,0.104],["this",0.151,0.313],["world,",0.383,0.871],["everyone",0.971,1.377],["inside",1.4,1.679],["the",1.702,1.772],["giant",1.83,2.12],["turtle",2.155,2.445],["has",2.468,2.573],["a",2.608,2.631],["drumbeat",2.677,3.095],["ticking",3.142,3.444],["in",3.502,3.548],["their",3.571,3.687],["wrist,",3.734,4.245],["except",4.419,4.814],["me.",4.907,5.324],["You",5.424,5